From edd at debian.org  Sat Apr 23 15:15:01 2022
From: edd at debian.org (Dirk Eddelbuettel)
Date: Sat, 23 Apr 2022 10:15:01 -0500
Subject: R 4.2.0 suggests a rebuild of graphics packages
Message-ID: <25188.6133.155978.426646@rob.eddelbuettel.com>

R 4.2.0 was released yesterday as scheduled.

Per the NEWS.Rd file [1] in the second section 'Grahphics' the first point is

  GRAPHICS

  The graphics engine version, R_GE_version, has been bumped to 15 and so
  packages that provide graphics devices should be reinstalled.

so packages providing a graphics device should be rebuilt. We discussed this
previously (as R 4.1.0 also updated the graphics device capabilities) and I
still think it is not worth defining a new r-api-* alike tag for this as it
really only affects a good handful of packages.

Dirk

[1] The web version is still at 4.1.3 as I just reported to r-devel so here is the
snippet via the GitHub mirror of the SVN sources:
https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/blob/master/doc/NEWS.Rd#L372-L376

-- 
dirk.eddelbuettel.com | @eddelbuettel | edd at debian.org

